      "writtenOn": "2021-06-30T17:36:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"someone else\" has to be a vendor or oem and they should know what they are doing. Let\u0027s use index \u003c 0 as the way to force an early return.\n\nI don\u0027t really like -EINVAL as the return since the caller didn\u0027t do anything wrong. Maybe the best would be:\n\n  if (index \u003c 0)\n    return index;\n    \nThen the hook can surface a reason (in case anyone cares). You can obviously implement your hook to return index \u003d\u003d -EINVAL if you want.",
